<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Constantine Dadeshkeliani</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1826">1826</a>–<a href="/years/1857">1857</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Constantine Dadeshkeliani was the last ruling prince of Svaneti in the Georgian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a>. Resisting the Russian authorities' plans to remove him, in 1857 he stabbed to death Prince Alexander Gagarin, the governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kutaisi">Kutaisi</a>, during a meeting. He was court-martialled and shot, and in 1858 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> abolished his principality.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/constantine-dadeshkeliani.jpg" alt="Constantine Dadeshkeliani" width="320" height="402" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Constantine_Dadeshkeliani,_Prince_of_Svaneti.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
